{"author_count":2,"contributors":["Møgelberg, Rasmus Ejlers","Vezzosi, Andrea"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382487"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"two guarded recursive powerdomains for applicative simulation","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4204/EPTCS.351.13","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382487","identifier":[{"id":"85122282218","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-5179a55e-5c0b-418b-85fc-c9300e8f1361"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-7F727F38E5D5667001EB73B6758255DE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4204/EPTCS.351.13","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus Ejlers","key":"møgelbergpau","last":"Møgelberg","locid":"10003d22-a201-4b64-88e3-b423bc76fcc2","name":"Møgelberg, Rasmus Ejlers","orcid":"0000-0003-0386-4376","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrea","key":"vezzosipau","last":"Vezzosi","name":"Vezzosi, Andrea","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4204/eptcs.351.13","pages":"200-217","publisher":"Electronic Proceedings in Theoretical Computer Science","status":"p","title":"Proceedings 37th Conference on Mathematical Foundations of Programming Semantics","volume":"351"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85122282218"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-5179a55e-5c0b-418b-85fc-c9300e8f1361"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Two Guarded Recursive Powerdomains for Applicative Simulation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382487","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"When designing languages for functional reactive programming (FRP) the main challenge is to provide the user with a simple, flexible interface for writing programs on a high level of abstraction while ensuring that all programs can be implemented efficiently in a low-level language. To meet this challenge, a new family of modal FRP languages has been proposed, in which variants of Nakano's guarded fixed point operator are used for writing recursive programs guaranteeing properties such as causality and productivity. As an apparent extension to this it has also been suggested to use Linear Temporal Logic (LTL) as a language for reactive programming through the Curry-Howard isomorphism, allowing properties such as termination, liveness and fairness to be encoded in types. However, these two ideas are in conflict with each other, since the fixed point operator introduces non-termination into the inductive types that are supposed to provide termination guarantees. In this paper we show that by regarding the modal time step operator of LTL a submodality of the one used for guarded recursion (rather than equating them), one can obtain a modal type system capable of expressing liveness properties while retaining the power of the guarded fixed point operator. We introduce the language Lively RaTT, a modal FRP language with a guarded fixed point operator and an `until' type constructor as in LTL, and show how to program with events and fair streams. Using a step-indexed Kripke logical relation we prove operational properties of Lively RaTT including productivity and causality as well as the termination and liveness properties expected of types from LTL. Finally, we prove that the type system of Lively RaTT guarantees the absence of implicit space leaks.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Bahr, Patrick","Graulund, Christian Uldal","Møgelberg, Rasmus Ejlers"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384887"],"event":{"acronym":"POPL","title":"ACM SIGPLAN Symposium on Principles of Programming Languages"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Curry Howard Isomorphism","Functional Reactive Programming","Guarded Recursion","Linear Temporal Logic","Modal Type Systems"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"diamonds are not forever liveness in reactive programming with guarded recursion","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3434283","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384887","identifier":[{"id":"85099045012","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-f57dac1e-2437-41b9-b7a7-2f50ead52087"],"keyword":["Curry-Howard Isomorphism","Functional Reactive Programming","Guarded Recursion","Linear Temporal Logic","Modal Type Systems"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2FBFB4DE073536D177B54DF32565A566"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85724929/diamondsnotforever.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3434283","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Patrick","key":"bahrpau","last":"Bahr","locid":"5e271e6a-7a91-47bd-9f12-3b73f4e0d7ac","name":"Bahr, Patrick","orcid":"0000-0003-1600-8261","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian Uldal","key":"graulundpau","last":"Graulund","name":"Graulund, Christian Uldal","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus Ejlers","key":"møgelbergpau","last":"Møgelberg","locid":"10003d22-a201-4b64-88e3-b423bc76fcc2","name":"Møgelberg, Rasmus Ejlers","orcid":"0000-0003-0386-4376","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3434283","edition":"POPL","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","series":"Proceedings of the ACM on Programming Languages","status":"p","title":"ACM SIGPLAN Symposium on Principles of Programming Languages","volume":"5"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85099045012"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-f57dac1e-2437-41b9-b7a7-2f50ead52087"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Diamonds are not forever: Liveness in reactive programming with guarded recursion","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384887","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Clocked Type Theory (CloTT) is a type theory for guarded recursion useful for programming with coinductive types, allowing productivity to be encoded in types, and for reasoning about advanced programming language features using an abstract form of step-indexing. CloTT has previously been shown to enjoy a number of syntactic properties including strong normalisation, canonicity and decidability of the equational theory. In this paper we present a denotational semantics for CloTT useful, e.g., for studying future extensions of CloTT with constructions such as path types. The main challenge for constructing this model is to model the notion of ticks on a clock used in CloTT for coinductive reasoning about coinductive types. We build on a category previously used to model guarded recursion with multiple clocks. In this category there is an object of clocks but no object of ticks, and so tick-assumptions in a context can not be modelled using standard tools. Instead we model ticks using dependent right adjoint functors, a generalisation of the category theoretic notion of adjunction to the setting of categories with families. Dependent right adjoints are known to model Fitch-style modal types, but in the case of CloTT, the modal operators constitute a family indexed internally in the type theory by clocks. We model this family using a dependent right adjoint on the slice category over the object of clocks. Finally we show how to model the tick constant of CloTT using a semantic substitution. This work improves on a previous model by the first two named authors which not only had a flaw but was also considerably more complicated.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Mannaa, Bassel","Møgelberg, Rasmus Ejlers","Veltri, Niccolò"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384270"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Estonia"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Tallinn University"],"keyword":["Coinductive Types","Denotational Semantics","Dependent type theory","Guarded Recursion","Modal Types"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["eToroX Labs"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ticking clocks as dependent right adjoints denotational semantics for clocked type theory","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.23638/LMCS-16(4:17)2020","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384270","identifier":[{"id":"85101631804","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-cd1f4806-d0b0-4622-9f7b-68b95fda7b46"],"keyword":["Coinductive Types","Denotational Semantics","Dependent Type Theory","Guarded Recursion","Modal Types"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-ECAD763C40323F09C07A09AED144319A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.23638/LMCS-16(4:17)2020","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85657507/CloTTModel.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["eToroX Labs"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"ee","key":"tallinn university","loc":["Estonia","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Tallinn University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bassel","key":"mannaapau","last":"Mannaa","name":"Mannaa, Bassel","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus Ejlers","key":"møgelbergpau","last":"Møgelberg","locid":"10003d22-a201-4b64-88e3-b423bc76fcc2","name":"Møgelberg, Rasmus Ejlers","orcid":"0000-0003-0386-4376","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Niccolò","key":"veltripau","last":"Veltri","name":"Veltri, Niccolò","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.23638/lmcs-16(4:17)2020","issn":["18605974"],"issue":"4","journal":"Logical Methods in Computer Science","paperid":"6278","publisher":"International Federation for Computational Logic","status":"p","title":"Logical Methods in Computer Science","volume":"16"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85101631804"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-cd1f4806-d0b0-4622-9f7b-68b95fda7b46"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Ticking clocks as dependent right adjoints: Denotational semantics for clocked type theory","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384270","year":"2020","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"In recent years, we have seen several new models of dependent type theory extended with some form of modal necessity operator, including nominal type theory, guarded and clocked type theory and spatial and cohesive type theory. In this paper, we study modal dependent type theory: dependent type theory with an operator satisfying (a dependent version of) the K axiom of modal logic. We investigate both semantics and syntax. For the semantics, we introduce categories with families with a dependent right adjoint (CwDRA) and show that the examples above can be presented as such. Indeed, we show that any category with finite limits and an adjunction of endofunctors give rise to a CwDRA via the local universe construction. For the syntax, we introduce a dependently typed extension of Fitch-style modal λ-calculus, show that it can be interpreted in any CwDRA, and build a term model. We extend the syntax and semantics with universes.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Birkedal, Lars","Clouston, Ranald","Mannaa, Bassel","Ejlers Møgelberg, Rasmus","Pitts, Andrew M.","Spitters, Bas"],"cuid":["S02-092.71-020660"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Mannaa, Bassel"],"country":["Australia","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Australian National University","University of Cambridge"],"keyword":["Category theory","Dependent type theory","Modal logic"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"modal dependent type theory and dependent right adjoints","src":["au","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84753867/paper.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-092.71-020660","identifier":[{"id":"85076567664","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-6d47a574-9aaa-4c69-8485-c8a490847236","itu-daf56809-22d1-4eb0-9b22-618c114e5e07"],"keyword":["Dependent type theory","category theory","modal logic"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-E1E6F283DD2692B0CBAA240DA91B3876"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84753867/paper.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1804.05236.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)","Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"au","key":"australian national university","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"Australian National University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Concordium Research ApS"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"gb","key":"university of cambridge","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Cambridge","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"birkedalpau","last":"Birkedal","locid":"bd012524-7d01-45f4-9bbd-8f8273bf14c7","name":"Birkedal, Lars","orcid":"0000-0003-1320-0098","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ranald","key":"cloustonpau","last":"Clouston","name":"Clouston, Ranald","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Bassel","key":"mannaapau","last":"Mannaa","name":"Mannaa, Bassel","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus Ejlers","key":"møgelbergpau","last":"Møgelberg","locid":"10003d22-a201-4b64-88e3-b423bc76fcc2","name":"Møgelberg, Rasmus Ejlers","orcid":"0000-0003-0386-4376","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrew M.","key":"pittspau","last":"Pitts","name":"Pitts, Andrew M.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrew","key":"mpittspau","last":"M. Pitts","name":"M. Pitts, Andrew","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bas","key":"spitterspau","last":"Spitters","locid":"50702ece-1b57-4820-9476-c6aad7c95d8f","name":"Spitters, Bas","orcid":"0000-0002-2802-0973","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1017/s0960129519000197","issn":["09601295","14698072"],"issn_org":["09601295"],"issue":"2","journal":"Mathematical Structures in Computer Science","pages"