{"abstract":"Building a static analyses for a real language involves modeling of large domains capturing the many available data types. To scale domain design and support efficient development of project-specific analyzers, it is desirable to be able to build, extend, and change abstractions in a systematic and modular fashion. We present a framework for modular design of abstract domains for recursive types and higher-order functions, based on the theory of solving recursive domain equations. We show how to relate computable abstract domains to our framework, and illustrate the potential of the construction by modularizing a monolithic domain for regular tree grammars. A prototype implementation in the dependently typed functional language Agda shows how the theoretical solution can be used in practice to construct static analysers.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Al-Sibahi, Ahmad Salim","Jensen, Thomas P.","Møgelberg, Rasmus Ejlers","Wasowski, Andrzej"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382218"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["France"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","The French National Institute for Computer Science (INRIA)"],"keyword":["Abstract Domains","Higher Order Functions","Modular design","Recursive Types","Static analysis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"galois connections for recursive types","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85385939/20191129_HankinFestschriftFinal.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382218","identifier":[{"id":"85079614059","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-404d2e4b-d22c-43e7-b0ea-8839802df00c"],"keyword":["Abstract Domains","Higher-Order Functions","Modular Design","Recursive Types","Static Analysis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-86AD94BA7E007C5880FA32680AD27223"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85385939/20191129_HankinFestschriftFinal.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"fr","key":"the french national institute for computer science","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"The French National Institute for Computer Science (INRIA)","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ahmad Salim","key":"alsibahipau","last":"Al-Sibahi","name":"Al-Sibahi, Ahmad Salim","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas P.","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Thomas P.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus Ejlers","key":"møgelbergpau","last":"Møgelberg","locid":"10003d22-a201-4b64-88e3-b423bc76fcc2","name":"Møgelberg, Rasmus Ejlers","orcid":"0000-0003-0386-4376","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrzej","key":"wasowskipau","last":"Wasowski","locid":"a39b94ff-e1b6-4b96-8404-486167a9123d","name":"Wasowski, Andrzej","orcid":"0000-0003-0532-2685","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-030-41103-9_4","eisbn":["9783030411039"],"isbn":["9783030411022"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"105-131","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","title":"From Lambda Calculus to Cybersecurity Through Program Analysis"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85079614059"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-404d2e4b-d22c-43e7-b0ea-8839802df00c"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Galois Connections for Recursive Types","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382218","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Building a static analyser for a real language involves modeling of large domains capturing the many available data types. To scale domain design and support efficient development of project-specific analyzers, it is desirable to be able to build, extend, and change abstractions in a systematic and modular fashion. We present a framework for modular design of abstract domains for recursive types and higher-order functions, based on the theory of solving recursive domain equations. We show how to relate computable abstract domains to our framework, and illustrate the potential of the construction by modularizing a monolithic domain for regular tree grammars. A prototype implementation in the dependently typed functional language Agda shows how the theoretical solution can be used in practice to construct static analysers.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Al-Sibahi, Ahmad Salim","Jensen, Thomas P.","Møgelberg, Rasmus Ejlers","Wąsowski, Andrzej"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-496711"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"galois connections for recursive types","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85079614059&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-496711","identifier":[{"id":"85079614059","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-ace27b3b-7699-48b3-8024-b7dcb1899847"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-86AD94BA7E007C5880FA32680AD27223"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Programming Languages and Theory of Computation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Ahmad Salim","key":"alsibahipau","last":"Al-Sibahi","locid":"38825f86-c661-4c74-9a7d-ceda7b918599","name":"Al-Sibahi, Ahmad Salim","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"c03e1b47-ab86-4d5f-af12-55bd4109d4cc","name":"Jensen, Thomas P.","name_org":"Jensen, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0002-4064-7170","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Rasmus Ejlers","key":"møgelbergpau","last":"Møgelberg","name":"Møgelberg, Rasmus Ejlers","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Andrzej","key":"wąsowskipau","last":"Wąsowski","name":"Wąsowski, Andrzej","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-030-41103-9_4","issn":["03029743"],"pages":"105-131","publisher":"Springer VS","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"Essays Dedicated to Chris Hankin on the Occasion of His Retirement","title":"sFrom Lambda Calculus to Cybersecurity Through Program Analysis"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85079614059"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-ace27b3b-7699-48b3-8024-b7dcb1899847"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Galois Connections for Recursive Types","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-496711","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"We present a new model of Guarded Dependent Type Theory (GDTT), a type theory with guarded recursion and multiple clocks in which one can program with, and reason about coinductive types. Productivity of recursively defined coinductive programs and proofs is encoded in types using guarded recursion, and can therefore be checked modularly, unlike the syntactic checks implemented in modern proof assistants. The model is based on a category of covariant presheaves over a category of time objects, and quantification over clocks is modelled using a presheaf of clocks. To model the clock irrelevance axiom, crucial for programming with coinductive types, types must be interpreted as presheaves orthogonal to the object of clocks. In the case of dependent types, this translates to a unique lifting condition similar to the one found in homotopy theoretic models of type theory. Since the universes defined by the standard Hofmann-Streicher construction in this model do not satisfy this property, the universes in GDTT must be indexed by contexts of clock variables. A large and technical part of the paper is devoted to showing that these can be constructed in such a way that inclusions between universes induced by inclusions of clock variable contexts commute on the nose with type operations on the universes.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Bizjak, Aleš","Møgelberg, Rasmus Ejlers"],"cuid":["S02-098.31-025679"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Møgelberg, Rasmus Ejlers"],"keyword":["Coinductive Types","Denotational Semantics","Guarded Recursion","Type Theory","cs LO"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"denotational semantics for guarded dependent type theory","src":["au","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85385789/DenotationalSemGDTT.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-098.31-025679","identifier":[{"id":"85085304429","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-b26e5732-d963-4dfe-83f8-e025cf0ee45f","itu-ec137504-b4d6-4bf4-837b-d860410358b3"],"keyword":["Type theory","coinductive types","cs.LO","denotational semantics","guarded recursion"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B3842D3D0BF5D58C54DEA1723C01CFE2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85385789/DenotationalSemGDTT.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1802.03744.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Aleš","key":"bizjakpau","last":"Bizjak","locid":"cb580bc8-d836-45ff-80e9-a9dfa61833d6","name":"Bizjak, Aleš","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus Ejlers","key":"møgelbergpau","last":"Møgelberg","locid":"10003d22-a201-4b64-88e3-b423bc76fcc2","name":"Møgelberg, Rasmus Ejlers","orcid":"0000-0003-0386-4376","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1017/s0960129520000080","issn":["09601295","14698072"],"issn_org":["09601295"],"issue":"4","journal":"Mathematical Structures in Computer Science","pages":"342-378","publisher":"Cambridge University Press","status":"p","title":"Mathematical Structures in Computer Science","volume":"30"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85085304429"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-b26e5732-d963-4dfe-83f8-e025cf0ee45f","itu-ec137504-b4d6-4bf4-837b-d860410358b3"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Denotational semantics for guarded dependent type theory","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-098.31-025679","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Functional reactive programming (FRP) is a paradigm for programming with signals and events, allowing the user to describe reactive programs on a high level of abstraction. For this to make sense, an FRP language must ensure that all programs are causal, and can be implemented without introducing space leaks and time leaks. To this end, some FRP languages do not give direct access to signals, but just to signal functions. Recently, modal types have been suggested as an alternative approach to ensuring causality in FRP languages in the synchronous case, giving direct access to the signal and event abstractions. This paper presents Simply RaTT, a new modal calculus for reactive programming. Unlike prior calculi, Simply RaTT uses a Fitch-style approach to modal types, which simplifies the type system and makes programs more concise. Echoing a previous result by Krishnaswami for a different language, we devise an operational semantics that safely executes Simply RaTT programs without space leaks. We also identify a source of time leaks present in other modal FRP languages: The unfolding of fixed points in delayed computations. The Fitch-style presentation allows an easy way to rules out these leaks, which appears not to be possible in the more traditional dual context approach.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Bahr, Patrick","Graulund, Christian Uldal","Møgelberg, Rasmus Ejlers"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382853"],"event":{"acronym":"ICFP","title":"ACM SIGPLAN International Conference on Functional Programming"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Causality","Fitch Style Calculus","Functional Reactive Programming","Modal Types","Operational semantics","Reactive Programming","Signal Functions","Space Leaks","Time Leaks","Type systems"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"simply ratt a fitch style modal calculus for reactive programming","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3341713","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382853","identifier":[{"id":"85085938198","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-69cb3ec2-c472-47e3-8eb9-08b5a6ed43ed"],"keyword":["Causality","Fitch-Style Calculus","Functional Reactive Programming","Modal Types","Operational Semantics","Reactive Programming","Signal Functions","Space Leaks","Time Leaks","Type Systems"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-90437D4336B3A7B39B54D1F97FDA8933"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84375815/icfp2019.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3341713","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Patrick","key":"bahrpau","last":"Bahr","locid":"5e271e6a-7a91-47bd-9f12-3b73f4e0d7ac","name":"Bahr, Patrick","orcid":"0000-0003-1600-8261","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian Uldal","key":"graulundpau","last":"Graulund","name":"Graulund, Christian Uldal","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus Ejlers","key":"møgelbergpau","last":"Møgelberg","locid":"10003d22-a201-4b64-88e3-b423bc76fcc2","name":"Møgelberg, Rasmus Ejlers","orcid":"0000-0003-0386-4376","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3341713","edition":"IFCP","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the ACM on Programming Languages","volume":"3"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85085938198"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-69cb3ec2-c472-47e3-8eb9-08b5a6ed43ed"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Simply RaTT: A Fitch-style Modal Calculus for Reactive Programming","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382853","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"In type theory, coinductive types are used to represent processes, and are thus crucial for the formal verification of non-terminating reactive programs in proof assistants based on type theory, such as Coq and Agda. Currently, programming and reasoning about coinductive types is difficult for two reasons: The need for recursive definitions to be productive, and the lack of coincidence of the built-in identity types and the important notion of bisimilarity. Guarded recursion in the sense of Nakano has recently been suggested as a possible approach to dealing with the problem of productivity, allowing this to be encoded in types. Indeed, coinductive types can be encoded using a combination of guarded recursion and universal quantification over clocks. This paper studies the notion of bisimilarity for guarded recursive types in Ticked Cubical Type Theory, an extension of Cubical Type Theory with guarded recursion. We prove that, for any functor, an abstract, category theoretic notion of bisimilarity for the final guarded coalgebra is equivalent (in the sense of homotopy type theory) to path equality (the primitive notion of equality in cubical type theory). As a worked example we study a guarded notion of labelled transition systems, and show that, as a special case of the general theorem, path equality coincides with an adaptation of the usual notion of bisimulation for processes. In particular, this implies that guarded recursion can be used to give simple equational reasoning proofs of bisimilarity. This work should be seen as a step towards obtaining bisimilarity as path equality for coinductive types using the encodings mentioned above.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Veltri, Niccolò","Møgelberg, Rasmus Ejlers"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382254"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Bisimilarity","Coinductive Types","Guarded Recursion","Labelled transition systems","Ticked Cubical Type Theory"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"bisimulation as path type for guarded recursive types","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3290317","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382254","identifier":[{"id":"85079466275","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-427bbe6d-d8d0-46dc-b2f9-8179ba4f0551"],"keyword":["Bisimilarity","Coinductive types","Guarded recursion","Labelled transition systems","Ticked Cubical Type Theory"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5BE5C3B41A3E904825878AAB4503D212"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3290317","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84061449/paper_arxiv.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Niccolò","key":"veltripau","last":"Veltri","name":"Veltri, Niccolò","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus Ejlers","key":"møgelbergpau","last":"Møgelberg","locid":"10003d22-a201-4b64-88e3-b423bc76fcc2","name":"Møgelberg, Rasmus Ejlers","orcid":"0000-0003-0386-4376","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3290317","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the ACM on Programming Languages","volume":"3"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85079466275"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-427bbe6d-d8d0-46dc-b2f9-8179ba4f0551"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Bisimulation as path type for guarded recursive types","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382254","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Clocked Type Theory (CloTT) is a type theory for guarded recursion useful for programming with coinductive types, allowing productivity to be encoded in types, and for reasoning about advanced programming language features using an abstract form of step-indexing. CloTT has previously been shown to enjoy a number of syntactic properties including strong normalisation, canonicity and decidability of type checking. In this paper we present a denotational semantics for CloTT useful, e.g., for studying future extensions of CloTT with constructions such as path types. The main challenge for constructing this model is to model the notion of ticks used in CloTT for coinductive reasoning about coinductive types. We build on a category previously used to model guarded recursion, but in this category there is no object of ticks, so tick-assumptions in a context can not be modelled using standard tools. Instead we show how ticks can be modelled using adjoint functors, and how to model the tick constant using a semantic substitution.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Mannaa, Bassel","Møgelberg, Rasmus Ejlers"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381685"],"event":{"acronym":"FSCD","title":"International Conference on Formal Structures for Computation and Deduction"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Clocked Type Theory","Coinductive Types","Denotational Semantics","Guarded Recursion","Step Indexing"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the clocks they are adjunctions denotational semantics for clocked type theory","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.FSCD.2018.23","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381685","identifier":[{"id":"85049781787","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-1bed90c2-9f6d-43dc-837d-d7687682859b"],"keyword":["Clocked Type Theory","Coinductive Types","Denotational Semantics","Guarded Recursion","Step-Indexing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-F2ACF2C33BD4244033DD557B27556468"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.FSCD.2018.23","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83273859/LIPIcs_FSCD_2018_23.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bassel","key":"mannaapau","last":"Mannaa","name":"Mannaa, Bassel","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus Ejlers","key":"møgelbergpau","last":"Møgelberg","locid":"10003d22-a201-4b64-88e3-b423bc76fcc2","name":"Møgelberg, Rasmus Ejlers","orcid":"0000-0003-0386-4376","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4230/lipics.fscd.2018.23","isbn":["9783959770774"],"issn":["18688969"],"publisher":"Schloss Dagstuhl - Leibniz-Zentrum fuer Informatik GmbH","series":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics","status":"p","title":"3rd International Conference on Formal Structures for Computation and Deduction (FSCD 2018)","volume":"108"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85049781787"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-1bed90c2-9f6d-43dc-837d-d7687682859b"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Clocks They Are Adjunctions: Denotational Semantics for Clocked Type Theory","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381685","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Just like any other branch of mathematics, denotational semantics of programming languages should be formalised in type theory, but adapting traditional domain theoretic semantics, as originally formulated in classical set theory to type theory has proven challenging. This paper is part of a project on formulating denotational semantics in type theories with guarded recursion. This should have the benefit of not only giving simpler semantics and proofs of properties such as adequacy, but also hopefully in the future to scale to languages with advanced features, such as general references, outside the reach of traditional domain theoretic techniques. Working in Guarded Dependent Type Theory (GDTT), we develop denotational semantics for Fixed Point Calculus (FPC), the simply typed lambda calculus extended with recursive types, modelling the recursive types of FPC using the guarded recursive types of GDTT. We prove soundness and computational adequacy of the model in GDTT using a logical relation between syntax and semantics constructed also using guarded recursive types. The denotational semantics is intensional in the sense that it counts the number of unfold-fold reductions needed to compute the value of a term, but we construct a relation relating the denotations of extensionally equal terms, i.e., pairs of terms that compute the same value in a different number of steps. Finally, we show how the denotational semantics of terms can be executed inside type theory and prove that executing the denotation of a boolean term computes the same value as the operational semantics of FPC.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Møgelberg, Rasmus Ejlers","Paviotti, Marco"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382638"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Kent"],"keyword":["Computational Adequacy","Denotational Semantics","Fixed Point Calculus FPC","Guarded Recursion","Type Theory"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"denotational semantics of recursive types in synthetic guarded domain theory","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83279675/1805.00289.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-382638","identifier":[{"id":"85047161057","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-5c14d286-5208-49af-afd8-56e30301a05f"],"keyword":["Computational Adequacy","Denotational Semantics","Fixed Point Calculus (FPC)","Guarded Recursion","Type Theory"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6E59B56E6DCB8ED1A72001679D44985C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1805.00289.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83279675/1805.00289.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of kent","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Kent","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus Ejlers","key":"møgelbergpau","last":"Møgelberg","locid":"10003d22-a201-4b64-88e3-b423bc76fcc2","name":"Møgelberg, Rasmus Ejlers","orcid":"0000-0003-0386-4376","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Marco","key":"paviottipau","last":"Paviotti","name":"Paviotti, Marco","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1017/s0960129518000087","issn":["09601295","14698072"],"issn_org":["09601295"],"journal":"Mathematical Structures in Computer Science","publisher":"Cambridge University Press","status":"p","title":"Mathematical Structures in Computer Science"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85047161057"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-5c14d286-5208-49af-afd8-56e30301a05f"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Denotational semantics of recursive types in synthetic guarded domain theory","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382638","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"We give an overview of the syntax and semantics of Clocked Type Theory (CloTT), a dependent type theory for guarded recursion with many clocks, in which one can encode coinductive types and capture the notion of productivity in types. The main novelty of CloTT is the notion of ticks, which allows one to open the delay type modality, and, e.g., define a dependent form of applicative functor action, which can be used for reasoning about coinductive data. In the talk we will give examples of programming and reasoning about guarded recursive and coinductive data in CloTT, and we will present the main syntactic results: Strong normalisation, canonicity and decidability of type checking. If time permits, we will also sketch the main ideas of the denotational semantics for CloTT.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Bahr, Patrick","Mannaa, Bassel","Møgelberg, Rasmus Ejlers"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381539"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Clocked Type Theory","Coinductive Types","Dependent type theory","Guarded Recursion","Productivity in Types"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"what makes guarded types tick","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83193673/abstract.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381539","ids":["itu-12439699-8505-496e-8aaf-73590fe86131"],"keyword":["Clocked Type Theory","Coinductive Types","Dependent Type Theory","Guarded Recursion","Productivity in Types"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-85710B1AD9C32A09D3C9424F88EC76B8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83193673/abstract.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Patrick","key":"bahrpau","last":"Bahr","locid":"5e271e6a-7a91-47bd-9f12-3b73f4e0d7ac","name":"Bahr, Patrick","orcid":"0000-0003-1600-8261","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bassel","key":"mannaapau","last":"Mannaa","name":"Mannaa, Bassel","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus Ejlers","key":"møgelbergpau","last":"Møgelberg","locid":"10003d22-a201-4b64-88e3-b423bc76fcc2","name":"Møgelberg, Rasmus Ejlers","orcid":"0000-0003-0386-4376","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-12439699-8505-496e-8aaf-73590fe86131"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"What makes guarded types tick?","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381539","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"author_count":3,"contributors":["Bahr, Patrick","Grathwohl, Hans Bugge","Møgelberg, Rasmus Ejlers"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-240402"],"event":{"end":"2017-06-23","place":"Reykjavik, is","start":"2017-06-20","title":"32nd Annual ACM/IEEE Symposium on Logic in Computer Science, LICS 2017","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the clocks are ticking no more delays","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85034057414","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-240402","identifier":[{"id":"85034057414","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-c2aa5deb-956f-4d2c-ba03-df5534010dd3"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-630D39E9BE1A1DA679D15C607A02073F"],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Patrick","key":"bahrpau","last":"Bahr","name":"Bahr, Patrick","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hans Bugge","key":"grathwohlpau","last":"Grathwohl","locid":"e8539989-3da2-47ac-b2b4-ed449ec6c230","name":"Grathwohl, Hans Bugge","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus Ejlers","key":"møgelbergpau","last":"Møgelberg","name":"Møgelberg, Rasmus Ejlers","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/lics.2017.8005097","eisbn":["9781509030187"],"issn":["10436871"],"issue":"32","publisher":"IEEE","series":"Annual Symposium on Logic in Computer Science","status":"p","title":"2017 32nd Annual ACM/IEEE Symposium on Logic in Computer Science, LICS 2017"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85034057414"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-c2aa5deb-956f-4d2c-ba03-df5534010dd3"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"The clocks are ticking : No more delays!","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-240402","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Guarded recursion in the sense of Nakano allows general recursive types and terms to be added to type theory without breaking consistency. Recent work has demonstrated applications of guarded recursion such as programming with codata, reasoning about coinductive types, as well as constructing and reasoning about denotational models of general recursive types. Guarded recursion can also be used as an abstract form of step-indexing for reasoning about programming languages with advanced features. Ultimately, we would like to have an implementation of a type theory with guarded recursion in which all these applications can be carried out and machine-checked. In this paper, we take a step towards this goal by devising a suitable reduction semantics. We present Clocked Type Theory, a new type theory for guarded recursion that is more suitable for reduction semantics than the existing ones. We prove confluence, strong normalisation and canonicity for its reduction semantics, constructing the theoretical basis for a future implementation. We show how coinductive types as exemplified by streams can be encoded, and derive that the type system ensures productivity of stream definitions.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Bahr, Patrick","Grathwohl, Hans Bugge","Møgelberg, Rasmus Ejlers"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382138"],"event":{"acronym":"LICS","title":"ACM/IEEE Symposium on Logic in Computer Science"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["type theory guarded recursion reduction semantics strong normalisation coinductive types recursive types"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the clocks are ticking no more delays reduction semantics for type theory with guarded recursion","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82163359/bahr17lics_paper.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382138","identifier":[{"id":"85034057414","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-3b6b9080-03bc-42d1-aac5-d6ae5413e329"],"keyword":["type theory, guarded recursion, reduction semantics, strong normalisation, coinductive types, recursive types"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-630D39E9BE1A1DA679D15C607A02073F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82163359/bahr17lics_paper.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Patrick","key":"bahrpau","last":"Bahr","locid":"5e271e6a-7a91-47bd-9f12-3b73f4e0d7ac","name":"Bahr, Patrick","orcid":"0000-0003-1600-8261","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Hans Bugge","key":"grathwohlpau","last":"Grathwohl","name":"Grathwohl, Hans Bugge","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus Ejlers","key":"møgelbergpau","last":"Møgelberg","locid":"10003d22-a201-4b64-88e3-b423bc76fcc2","name":"Møgelberg, Rasmus Ejlers","orcid":"0000-0003-0386-4376","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/lics.2017.8005097","issn":["10436871"],"journal":"Annual Symposium on Logic in Computer Science","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"Annual Symposium on Logic in Computer Science"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85034057414"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-3b6b9080-03bc-42d1-aac5-d6ae5413e329"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Clocks Are Ticking: No More Delays! : Reduction Semantics for Type Theory with Guarded Recursion","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382138","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Guarded recursion is a form of recursion where recursive calls are guarded by delay modalities. Previous work has shown how guarded recursion is useful for reasoning operationally about programming languages with advanced features including general references, recursive types, countable non-determinism and concurrency. Guarded recursion also offers a way of adding recursion to type theory while maintaining logical consistency. In previous work we initiated a programme of denotational semantics in type theory using guarded recursion, by constructing a computationally adequate model of the language PCF (simply typed lambda calculus with fixed points). This model was intensional in that it could distinguish between computations computing the same result using a different number of fixed point unfoldings. In this work we show how also programming languages with recursive types can be given denotational semantics in type theory with guarded recursion. More precisely, we give a computationally adequate denotational semantics to the language FPC (simply typed lambda calculus extended with recursive types), modelling recursive types using guarded recursive types. The model is intensional in the same way as was the case in previous work, but we show how to recover extensionality using a logical relation. All constructions and reasoning in this paper, including proofs of theorems such as soundness and adequacy, are by (informal) reasoning in type theory, often using guarded recursion.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Møgelberg, Rasmus Ejlers","Paviotti, Marco"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384714"],"event":{"acronym":"LICS","title":"ACM/IEEE Symposium on Logic in Computer Science"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Computational Adequacy","Denotational Semantics","Guarded Recursion","Recursive Types","Type Theory"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"denotational semantics of recursive types in synthetic guarded domain theory","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81547566/p317_Mogelberg.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384714","identifier":[{"id":"84994578230","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-e9c72644-2f84-4456-8467-8ec411cf10e1"],"keyword":["Computational Adequacy","Denotational Semantics","Guarded Recursion","Recursive Types","Type Theory"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-EDFA6E939F44E85D42967321D96FBB6E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81547566/p317_Mogelberg.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics","The Department, Theoretical Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus Ejlers","key":"møgelbergpau","last":"Møgelberg","locid":"10003d22-a201-4b64-88e3-b423bc76fcc2","name":"Møgelberg, Rasmus Ejlers","orcid":"0000-0003-0386-4376","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marco","key":"paviottipau","last":"Paviotti","name":"Paviotti, Marco","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/2933575.2934516","isbn":["9781450343916"],"pages":"317-326","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"LICS '16 Proceedings of the 31st Annual ACM/IEEE Symposium on Logic in Computer Science"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84994578230"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-e9c72644-2f84-4456-8467-8ec411cf10e1"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Denotational semantics of recursive types in synthetic guarded domain theory","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384714","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"We present guarded dependent type theory, gDTT, an extensional dependent type theory with a ‘later’ modality and clock quantifiers for programming and proving with guarded recursive and coinductive types. The later modality is used to ensure the productivity of recursive definitions in a modular, type based, way. Clock quantifiers are used for controlled elimination of the later modality and for encoding coinductive types using guarded recursive types. Key to the development of gDTT are novel type and term formers involving what we call ‘delayed substitutions’. These generalise the applicative functor rules for the later modality considered in earlier work, and are crucial for programming and proving with dependent types. We show soundness of the type theory with respect to a denotational model.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Bizjak, Aleš","Grathwohl, Hans Bugge","Clouston, Ranald","Møgelberg, Rasmus E.","Birkedal, Lars"],"cuid":["S02-082.05-029835"],"event":{"acronym":"FoSSaCS","end":"2016-04-08","place":"Eindhoven, nl","start":"2016-04-02","title":"19th International Conference on Foundations of Software Science and Computation Structures, FOSSACS 2016 and Held as Part of the European Joint Conferences on Theory and Practice of Software, ETAPS 2016","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Bizjak, Aleš"],"keyword":["Coinductive Types","clock quantifiers","guarded dependent type theory","guarded recursive types","later modality"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"guarded dependent type theory with coinductive types","src":["au","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82370381/gdtt.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-082.05-029835","identifier":[{"id":"84961705072","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-ecb90513-dc24-4d00-b50d-83613716454b","itu-56bc7bd7-3841-40c5-909d-69a54abc46be"],"keyword":["clock quantifiers","coinductive types","guarded dependent type theory","guarded recursive types","later modality"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-6-E3E0368ADCBB4B8989BAD820C4777E97"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82370381/gdtt.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics","The Department, Theoretical Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Aleš","key":"bizjakpau","last":"Bizjak","locid":"cb580bc8-d836-45ff-80e9-a9dfa61833d6","name":"Bizjak, Aleš","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hans Bugge","key":"grathwohlpau","last":"Grathwohl","locid":"e8539989-3da2-47ac-b2b4-ed449ec6c230","name":"Grathwohl, Hans Bugge","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ranald","key":"cloustonpau","last":"Clouston","locid":"5082976b-e829-4130-8c97-c7f8dd88f90e","name":"Clouston, Ranald","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus Ejlers","key":"møgelbergpau","last":"Møgelberg","locid":"10003d22-a201-4b64-88e3-b423bc76fcc2","name":"Møgelberg, Rasmus Ejlers","orcid":"0000-0003-0386-4376","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"birkedalpau","last":"Birkedal","locid":"bd012524-7d01-45f4-9bbd-8f8273bf14c7","name":"Birkedal, Lars","orcid":"0000-0003-1320-0098","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Bart","key":"jacobspedh","last":"Jacobs","name":"Jacobs, Bart","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Christof","key":"lödingpedh","last":"Löding","name":"Löding, Christof","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-662-49630-5_2","eisbn":["9783662496305"],"isbn":["9783662496299"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"20-35","publisher":"Springer VS","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"19th International Conference, FOSSACS 2016","title":"Foundations of Software Science and Computation Structures","volume":"9634"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84961705072"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-ecb90513-dc24-4d00-b50d-83613716454b","itu-56bc7bd7-3841-40c5-909d-69a54abc46be"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Guarded Dependent Type Theory with Coinductive Types","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-082.05-029835","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"We present guarded dependent type theory, gDTT, an extensional dependent type theory with a later' modality and clock quantifiers for programming and proving with guarded recursive and coinductive types. The later modality is used to ensure the productivity of recursive definitions in a modular, type based, way. Clock quantifiers are used for controlled elimination of the later modality and for encoding coinductive types using guarded recursive types. Key to the development of gDTT are novel type and term formers involving what we call delayed substitutions’. These generalise the applicative functor rules for the later modality considered in earlier work, and are crucial for programming and proving with dependent types. We show soundness of the type theory with respect to a denotational model.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Bizjak, Aleš","Grathwohl, Hans Bugge","Clouston, Ranald","Birkedal, Lars","Møgelberg, Rasmus Ejlers"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-191885"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"guarded dependent type theory with coinductive types","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://arxiv.org/abs/1601.01586","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-191885","identifier":[{"id":"84961705072","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-6dad862a-8cf4-4366-9dc3-ba46999af3de"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-6-E3E0368ADCBB4B8989BAD820C4777E97"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Aleš","key":"bizjakpau","last":"Bizjak","locid":"cb580bc8-d836-45ff-80e9-a9dfa61833d6","name":"Bizjak, Aleš","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hans Bugge","key":"grathwohlpau","last":"Grathwohl","locid":"e8539989-3da2-47ac-b2b4-ed449ec6c230","name":"Grathwohl, Hans Bugge","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ranald","key":"cloustonpau","last":"Clouston","locid":"5082976b-e829-4130-8c97-c7f8dd88f90e","name":"Clouston, Ranald","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"birkedalpau","last":"Birkedal","locid":"bd012524-7d01-45f4-9bbd-8f8273bf14c7","name":"Birkedal, Lars","orcid":"0000-0003-1320-0098","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus Ejlers","key":"møgelbergpau","last":"Møgelberg","name":"Møgelberg, Rasmus Ejlers","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-662-49630-5_2","eisbn":["9783662496305"],"isbn":["9783662496299"],"issn":["03029743"],"publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","title":"Foundations of Software Science and Computation Structures"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84961705072"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-6dad862a-8cf4-4366-9dc3-ba46999af3de"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Guarded dependent type theory with coinductive types","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-191885","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Guarded recursion is an approach to solving recursive type equations where the type variable appears guarded by a modality to be thought of as a delay for one time step. Atkey and McBride proposed a calculus in which guarded recursion can be used when programming with coinductive data, allowing productivity to be captured in types. The calculus uses clocks representing time streams and clock quantifiers which allow limited and controlled elimination of modalities. The calculus has since been extended to dependent types by Møgelberg. Both works give denotational semantics but no rewrite semantics. In previous versions of this calculus, different clocks represented separate time streams and clock synchronisation was prohibited. In this paper we show that allowing clock synchronisation is safe by constructing a new model of guarded recursion and clocks. This result will greatly simplify the type theory by removing freshness restrictions from typing rules, and is a necessary step towards defining rewrite semantics, and ultimately implementing the calculus.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Bizjak, Aleš","Møgelberg, Rasmus Ejlers"],"cuid":["S02-089.36-013012"],"event":{"acronym":"MFPS","end":"2015-06-25","place":"Nijmegen, nl","start":"2015-06-22","title":"Conference on the Mathematical Foundations of Programming Semantics","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Categorical semantics","Coinductive Types","Guarded Recursion","Type Theory"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a model of guarded recursion with clock synchronisation","src":["au","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.entcs.2015.12.007","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-089.36-013012","identifier":[{"id":"84951830208","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-05a28165-fb0c-448e-9b0b-2309250d6c5d","itu-e196493c-b75c-4f4c-89f0-6bc2bca4ac58"],"keyword":["Guarded recursion","categorical semantics","coinductive types","type theory"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-94939ED12A4F050329CC18204A8BC218"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.entcs.2015.12.007","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1571066115000742","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.itu.dk/people/mogel/papers/clocks-mfps2015.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/80617588/clocks_mfps2015.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics","The Department, Theoretical Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Aleš","key":"bizjakpau","last":"Bizjak","locid":"cb580bc8-d836-45ff-80e9-a9dfa61833d6","name":"Bizjak, Aleš","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus Ejlers","key":"møgelbergpau","last":"Møgelberg","locid":"10003d22-a201-4b64-88e3-b423bc76fcc2","name":"Møgelberg, Rasmus Ejlers","orcid":"0000-0003-0386-4376","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.entcs.2015.12.007","issn":["15710661"],"journal":"Electronic Notes in Theoretical Computer Science","pages":"83-101","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"Electronic Notes in Theoretical Computer Science","volume":"319"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84951830208"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-05a28165-fb0c-448e-9b0b-2309250d6c5d","itu-e196493c-b75c-4f4c-89f0-6bc2bca4ac58"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A model of guarded recursion with clock synchronisation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-089.36-013012","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Guarded recursion is a form of recursion where recursive calls are guarded by delay modalities. Previous work has shown how guarded recursion is useful for constructing logics for reasoning about programming languages with advanced features, as well as for constructing and reasoning about elements of coinductive types. In this paper we investigate how type theory with guarded recursion can be used as a metalanguage for denotational semantics useful both for constructing models and for proving properties of these. We do this by constructing a fairly intensional model of PCF and proving it computationally adequate. The model construction is related to Escardo's metric model for PCF, but here everything is carried out entirely in type theory with guarded recursion, including the formulation of the operational semantics, the model construction and the proof of adequacy","author_count":3,"contributors":["Paviotti, Marco","Møgelberg, Rasmus Ejlers","Birkedal, Lars"],"cuid":["S02-090.08-022759"],"event":{"acronym":"MFPS","end":"2015-06-25","place":"Nijmegen, nl","start":"2015-06-22","title":"Conference on the Mathematical Foundations of Programming Semantics","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Denotational Semantics","Guarded Recursion","PCF","Type Theory","synthetic domain theory"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a model of pcf in guarded type theory","src":["au","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.entcs.2015.12.020","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-090.08-022759","identifier":[{"id":"84951760214","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-8a976773-99b4-481c-85bb-9039a0eecd3c","itu-019b8a7e-08f7-43cc-8450-c5905768b8a5"],"keyword":["Denotational semantics","PCF","guarded recursion","synthetic domain theory","type theory"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-F937F79C8E65E711444FB8EDFE35A0FB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/80617546/PCF_mfps2015.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://ac.els-cdn.com/S1571066115000870/1-s2.0-S1571066115000870-main.pdf?_tid=a4c46716-e1f0-11e5-a6f1-00000aacb35f&acdnat=1457086117_fbdf2f93fbe709a27b95beb7c41db3f5","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/98165643/pcf_in_s.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.entcs.2015.12.020","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://events.cs.bham.ac.uk/mfps31/mfpsproc.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics","The Department, Theoretical Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null